   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 674 of the laws of 1993, amending the public buildings\nlaw relating to value limitations on contracts, in relation to extending such\nprovisions thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8230",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8230-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 674 of 1993",
    "lawSection": "Public Buildings",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8230\n\nSPONSOR: BASKIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 674 of the laws of 1993, amending the public\nbuildings law relating to value limitations on contracts, in relation to\nextending such provisions thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to extend existing statutory authorization\nallowing emergency contracts to exceed standard value limits through\nJune 30, 2028.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one:\n\n*Extends the expiration date of Chapter 674 of the Laws of 1993, moving\nit from June 30, 2025, to June 30, 2028.\n\nSection two is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is needed to extend the law that allows state agencies to\nexceed standard contract value limits when responding to emergencies,\nsuch as major infrastructure failures, severe weather events, or urgent\nsupply needs. These provisions ensure agencies can act quickly to\nprotect public safety, maintain essential services, and prevent further\nharm or disruption. Without this extension, the authority would expire,\npotentially slowing emergency response and putting communities at risk.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTBD\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
